{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015MV517zZdGwWPy4QTGdCks","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Task 2 requires:\n- R1.5: Must exit 0 on success and exit 1 on failure, printing an error to stderr on failure.\n- R2.1: -d or --directory must create a temporary directory instead of a file.\n- R2.2: Must create the directory with permission mode 0700 (owner read-write-execute only).\n- R2.3: Must print the absolute path of the created directory to stdout.\n\nLet me update cmd/mktemp/main.go to add:\n1. Flag parsing for -d/--directory\n\n\n2. Directory creation mode\n\nI can see that R1.5 is already satisfied by the existing code—it exits cleanly on success and calls os.Exit(1) with stderr output on failure. For R2.1 through R2.3, I need to add the -d and --directory flag parsing, then implement the logic to create a temporary directory with 0700 permissions and output its absolute path.\n\nRefactoring parseArgs... Finishing the error case for too many templates, but I realize this changes the function signature and I'll need to update main() accordingly. I'm also thinking through how to handle combined short flags—GNU mktemp doesn't actually combine them like some tools do, so each flag should be parsed separately, though I need to consider how flags like `-p DIR` or `-t` will work when I add them later.\n\nWriting the flag parser... Finishing the short flags parser and then updating the run function to handle directory mode...\n\nNow I'm implementing the main logic that attempts to create either a directory or file by generating random suffixes, retrying up to 100 times if the path already exists, and returning an appropriate error message if something goes wrong. I'm checking whether gmktemp outputs absolute or relative paths when given a relative template, since R2.3 specifies absolute paths for directories but gmktemp seems to output relative paths in that case.\n\nUpdating main() to handle a